  "crossDomainRules": [
    "Article, post, video metadata, gallery, live metadata and series use the same content lifecycle contract unless a domain-specific state machine is explicitly approved.",
    "Actual media bytes are owned by the Media domain; Content stores only validated media references and metadata needed for content projection.",
    "Publishing is a state transition, not a boolean field mutation.",
    "Moderation approval is a policy-controlled transition and cannot be bypassed by directly setting PUBLISHED.",
    "Public Edge Cache may only contain the public projection of content that is currently cacheable.",
    "Every authoritative content mutation has one bounded D1 write; projections, search, counters and notifications are asynchronous.",
    "Payload collection CRUD never becomes public API automatically."
  ]
